":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"d6b13ab4-e32b-4eff-8c06-713aef815ac1\",\"uuid\":\"77dc179a-f6de-4f86-9d62-bf519d1eb7c5\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T17:20:09.258Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgiGhZTjg1XSVdL8aZZWy\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":1078,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgiGhZh8f77a6DxrGKoni\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I'll read TASK.md first, then follow what it says.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":30677,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":25508,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":30677},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"d6b13ab4-e32b-4eff-8c06-713aef815ac1\",\"uuid\":\"64c06248-5a91-4d3c-bb47-450ac5e9bfc1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T17:20:09.814Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgiGhZTjg1XSVdL8aZZWy\"}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgiGhZh8f77a6DxrGKoni\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01B2xxRLnnQQwrV5jj3w6r8K\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"$WSROOT/laya/s0/fable-high-r2/step1/TASK.md\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":30677,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":25508,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":30677},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"d6b13ab4-e32b-4eff-8c06-713aef815ac1\",\"uuid\":\"a62e5c16-3b9b-46c4-9622-19f245254800\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T17:20:11.488Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgiGhZTjg1XSVdL8aZZWy\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01B2xxRLnnQQwrV5jj3w6r8K\":{\"file_path\":\"$WSROOT/laya/s0/fable-high-r2/step1/TASK.md\"}}}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01B2xxRLnnQQwrV5jj3w6r8K\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Weight-editing task (step 1 of 3)\\n2\\t\\n3\\tYou are editing part of a neural network BY HAND. Do not train it.\\n4\\t\\n5\\t## The model\\n6\\tLaya is a decision model. For a customer message it routes to one of 5 support\\n7\\tdepartments: cards, disputes, transfers_topups, fees_fx, account_security. A frozen encoder turns (message, option) into one\\n8\\t1024-number vector per option (the \\\"marker vector\\\"). A small scorer gives each\\n9\\toption a logit; the highest logit wins. You edit ONLY the scorer.\\n10\\t\\n11\\t- `scorer_in.npz`: scorer weights. Scorer = LayerNorm(ln_w, ln_b) -> W1 (1024x1024),\\n12\\t  b1 -> GELU -> W2 (1024x1), b2. You may also add a ReLU module on the raw marker\\n13\\t  vector: arrays extra_W0, extra_b0, extra_W1, extra_b1, ... (ReLU between layers,\\n14\\t  last layer has 1 output); its output is added to the logit.\\n15\\t- `scorer.py`: `load`, `save`, `logits(S, M)`, `predict(S, M)`.\\n16\\t- `embed.py`: run the frozen encoder on messages you write yourself:\\n17\\t  `<lab>/.venv/bin/python embed.py out.npz \\\"message\\\" ...` -> out.npz with M [n, 5, 1024].\\n18\\t- `evidence.csv` + `evidence_M.npz`: 32 labelled customer messages for this\\n19\\t  correction and their marker vectors (same order).\\n20\\tUse this Python, which has numpy and torch: `<lab>/.venv/bin/python`\\n21\\t\\n22\\t## Department descriptions given to the model\\n23\\t- cards: getting, activating, delivering, replacing or using a payment card; PIN, contactless, virtual and disposable cards, Apple Pay or Google Pay, lost or stolen cards\\n24\\t- disputes: a payment, withdrawal or debit the customer does not recognise, was declined, is pending, was charged twice or reverted; refunds\\n25\\t- transfers_topups: sending or receiving money, bank transfers, topping up the account, balance not updated after a transfer or deposit\\n26\\t- fees_fx: fees and charges, exchange rates, currency exchange, supported currencies\\n27\\t- account_security: identity verification, passcode, personal details, closing the account, lost phone, age or country eligibility\\n28\\t\\n29\\t## Corrections already applied in earlier steps (must stay true)\\n30\\t(none)\\n31\\t\\n32\\t## New correction for this step\\n33\\tComplaints that a card payment or a cash withdrawal used a bad or wrong exchange rate belong to fees_fx, not disputes, even when the customer says the amount looks wrong.\\n34\\t\\n35\\t## What to do\\n36\\tWrite `scorer_out.npz` (same format) so that the model:\\n37\\t1. follows the new correction for all such messages, not only the examples;\\n38\\t2. still follows every earlier correction;\\n39\\t3. otherwise routes exactly as `scorer_in.npz` does.\\n40\\tA hidden test set of 3,080 real customer messages scores all three.\\n41\\t\\n42\\t## Rules\\n43\\t- Allowed: read weights, run the scorer and the encoder on inputs you choose,\\n44\\t  reason about directions and units, change any scorer weights, add the extra module.\\n45\\t- Not allowed: gradient descent, optimizers, any training or fitting loop,\\n46\\t  least squares, logistic regression or any solver fitted to data. Every weight\\n47\\t  you write must come from your own reasoning. Computing a direction as a\\n48\\t  difference of means of marker vectors of messages YOU wrote is allowed;\\n49\\t  fitting to the evidence labels is not. Checking with forward passes is fine.\\n50\\t- Write `NOTES.md`: what you changed and why, in under 200 words.\\n51\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"d6b13ab4-e32b-4eff-8c06-713aef815ac1\",\"uuid\":\"00090c30-37fd-464f-9944-d642d5f681be\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T17:20:11.499Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"$WSROOT/laya/s0/fable-high-r2/step1/TASK.md\",\"content\":\"# Weight-editing task (step 1 of 3)\\n\\nYou are editing part of a neural network BY HAND. Do not train it.\\n\\n## The model\\nLaya is a decision model. For a customer message it routes to one of 5 support\\ndepartments: cards, disputes, transfers_topups, fees_fx, account_security. A frozen encoder turns (message, option) into one\\n1024-number vector per option (the \\\"marker vector\\\"). A small scorer gives each\\noption a logit; the highest logit wins. You edit ONLY the scorer.\\n\\n- `scorer_in.npz`: scorer weights. Scorer = LayerNorm(ln_w, ln_b) -> W1 (1024x1024),\\n  b1 -> GELU -> W2 (1024x1), b2. You may also add a ReLU module on the raw marker\\n  vector: arrays extra_W0, extra_b0, extra_W1, extra_b1, ... (ReLU between layers,\\n  last layer has 1 output); its output is added to the logit.\\n- `scorer.py`: `load`, `save`, `logits(S, M)`, `predict(S, M)`.\\n- `embed.py`: run the frozen encoder on messages you write yourself:\\n  `<lab>/.venv/bin/python embed.py out.npz \\\"message\\\" ...` -> out.npz with M [n, 5, 1024].\\n- `evidence.csv` + `evidence_M.npz`: 32 labelled customer messages for this\\n  correction and their marker vectors (same order).\\nUse this Python, which has numpy and torch: `<lab>/.venv/bin/python`\\n\\n## Department descriptions given to the model\\n- cards: getting, activating, delivering, replacing or using a payment card; PIN, contactless, virtual and disposable cards, Apple Pay or Google Pay, lost or stolen cards\\n- disputes: a payment, withdrawal or debit the customer does not recognise, was declined, is pending, was charged twice or reverted; refunds\\n- transfers_topups: sending or receiving money, bank transfers, topping up the account, balance not updated after a transfer or deposit\\n- fees_fx: fees and charges, exchange rates, currency exchange, supported currencies\\n- account_security: identity verification, passcode, personal details, closing the account, lost phone, age or country eligibility\\n\\n## Corrections already applied in earlier steps (must stay true)\\n(none)\\n\\n## New correction for this step\\nComplaints that a card payment or a cash withdrawal used a bad or wrong exchange rate belong to fees_fx, not disputes, even when the customer says the amount looks wrong.\\n\\n## What to do\\nWrite `scorer_out.npz` (same format) so that the model:\\n1. follows the new correction for all such messages, not only the examples;\\n2. still follows every earlier correction;\\n3. otherwise routes exactly as `scorer_in.npz` does.\\nA hidden test set of 3,080 real customer messages scores all three.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Allowed: read weights, run the scorer and the encoder on inputs you choose,\\n  reason about directions and units, change any scorer weights, add the extra module.\\n- Not allowed: gradient descent, optimizers, any training or fitting loop,\\n  least squares, logistic regression or any solver fitted to data. Every weight\\n  you write must come from your own reasoning. Computing a direction as a\\n  difference of means of marker vectors of messages YOU wrote is allowed;\\n  fitting to the evidence labels is not. Checking with forward passes is fine.\\n- Write `NOTES.md`: what you changed and why, in under 200 words.\\n\",\"numLines\":51,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":51}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01B2xxRLnnQQwrV5jj3w6r8K\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"rule\"}}]}\n{\"type\":\"rate_limit_event\",\"rate_limit_info\":{\"status\":\"allowed\",\"resetsAt\":1794308400,\"rateLimitType\":\"seven_day\",\"overageStatus\":\"rejected\",\"overageDisabledReason\":\"org_level_disabled\",\"isUsingOverage\":false,\"unifiedWindows\":{\"seven_day\":{\"utilization\":0.25,\"resetsAt\":1794308400,\"status\":\"allowed\"},\"seven_day_overage_included\":{\"utilization\":0.14,\"resetsAt\":1794308400,\"status\":\"allowed\"}}},\"uuid\":\"944d96d2-67e9-49b2-8400-79714a461a8f\",\"session_id\":\"d6b13ab4-e32b-4eff-8c06-713aef815ac1\"}\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_summary\",\"detail\":\"Reading TASK.md\",\"uuid\":\"2f86dfaa-4f48-4380-a340-37994f64d3ee\",\"session_id\":\"d6b13ab4-e32b-4eff-8c06-713aef815ac1\"}\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"d6b13ab4-e32b-4eff-8c06-713aef815ac1\",\"uuid\":\"4fbe1d47-ab95-467a-8f50-cfa6258f4067\"}","numLines":18,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30,"truncatedByTokenCap":true}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013fNEdSZ5TYnFpT9o9gvLYz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
