{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgiJopYjyaVVwvLmDWUmy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Done.** `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` are written in the task directory. Evidence accuracy went from 16/32 to 30/32, with no original weight changed.\n\n**→ What I built.** A small ReLU \"extra\" module on the raw marker vector. It adds a boost to the fees_fx logit only when two conditions both hold: the vector looks like the **fees_fx option of an exchange-rate complaint**, and it looks like a **complaint rather than a currency question**. The AND is a `min(a, b)` built from three ReLU layers, times gain 3. Everywhere else the output is exactly zero, so other routing is bit-identical (verified: 17 zero-boost evidence rows match the original logits exactly).\n\n**→ Where the directions came from.** About 300 messages I wrote myself, embedded with the frozen encoder. Both directions are differences of means. The key trick: raw vectors are swamped by about 80 message-specific nuisance components (label-free PCA of option-averaged vectors). Projecting those out took the separation from near-random to usable. Thresholds sit at class-mean midpoints with small principled shifts.\n\n**→ Checks, all forward passes, held-out messages never used in any mean:**\n\n| Set | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Evidence (32) | 16 → 30 correct, 0 non-FX flips |\n| Held-out FX complaints (25) | 24 now fees_fx |\n| Disputes + other depts (145) | 1 flip |\n| Currency questions (60) | 8 flips, all ones the base already misrouted |\n\n**→ Known limits.** Two evidence misses remain: \"charged the wing amount for an item\" (no exchange-rate content at all) and one with a very large baseline deficit. The main hidden-set risk is **currency questions the baseline misroutes**: the complaint-vs-question factor is the weaker of the two, so some of those will flip to fees_fx. I judged that cost smaller than the recall lost by tightening it.\n\n**Also found:** the five option vectors of a message are mostly shared nuisance plus a per-option \"match quality\" signal, and option identity is barely encoded in a single vector. That shaped the design: no option gate is possible, so specificity has to come from the content directions."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":902,"cache_read_input_tokens":278118,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":902},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6b13ab4-e32b-4eff-8c06-713aef815ac1","uuid":"bab1e2d0-f738-4ebc-8e99-5954d7961dd8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T17:47:58.364Z","request_id":"req_011CgiJopFPb66NwiwkjQfkb"}
